<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kalidasa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kalidasa was a classical <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> poet and dramatist, widely regarded as the greatest writer in the language. His works include the drama Abhijnanashakuntalam and the poem Meghaduta. He is traditionally associated with the Gupta period and is a major part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gupta-empire">Gupta Empire</a>'s cultural legacy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kalidasa.jpg" alt="Kalidasa" width="293" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: William Douglas Almond · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kalidasa_inditing_the_cloud_Messenger,_A.D._375.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
